<SddRouter keywords="sdd, router, entry, intent, scale, route, stateless" type="directive" ver="2.3">
  <Mission>
    Route one operator intent from one read-only `sdd-state` snapshot to exactly one owner. The
    router writes no artifacts and maintains no persistent session. Durable artifacts and current
    repository state are the only continuation context.
  </Mission>
  <BeliefState>
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-language"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-tool-invocation"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-dialogue-style"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-dialogue-discipline"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-safeguard"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-no-process-narration"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-operator-output-live-text"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-diverge-before-recommend"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-scale-proportional-depth"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-stateless-flow"}}
    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-stateless-artifact"}}
    <Axiom id="AX_READER_WITHOUT_SESSION_CONTEXT" cross-cutting="true">
      Repo artifacts (specs, tickets, Decision Log entries) outlive the session that wrote them and
      are read by someone with zero memory of it. Before writing artifact text, apply the reader
      test: would an engineer who never saw this session understand it and act on it? Session-plan
      labels, «оператор попросил» as a justification, «рабочий дифф» meaning this session's working
      set — forbidden in artifacts; they belong to the session log. Introduce every term inline
      before using it. The artifact explains the thing; it never reports the work of making it.
    </Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_DECISION_LOG_NON_OBVIOUS" cross-cutting="true">
      A Decision Log entry is insider information for a future agent — the «why THIS way» it could
      not derive from the task alone: a real alternative rejected, an accepted risk, an operator's
      explicit exception to a rule, a deliberately non-optimal choice. Obvious rationale («split for
      readability», «named constant instead of a magic number») is noise that buries the genuine
      entries — fold it into a one-line reason at the entity (e.g. `Usage Waiver`) or drop it.

      A tool/technology pick already recorded in its own table or section of the spec (Tool Stack,
      Verification Commands, dependency list) is NEVER also a Decision Log entry — the table already
      is the record, and a DL row that just restates row `X → tool Y` is pure duplication, not insider
      information. DL is reserved for the pick that needed a real trade-off behind it: a choice that
      looks wrong until you know the constraint that forced it, a rejected alternative worth naming so
      nobody re-proposes it, a risk the operator knowingly accepted, or an explicit exception to a
      standing rule. Test before writing any entry: «could a future agent reading only the spec's own
      tables and prose re-derive this decision on its own?» — yes → do not write a DL entry, the spec
      already carries it; no (there is a real compromise, rejection, or risk that only the operator's
      reasoning explains) → DL entry.
    </Axiom>
    <Axiom id="AX_V2_HAS_NO_INTERNAL_MIGRATION">
      `sdd-migrate` is exclusively the explicit V1→V2 boundary. Invalid or stale V2 artifacts return
      to their owning V2 authoring flow. Never invent V2→V2 migration, schema upgrade, compatibility
      route, or migration session.
    </Axiom>
  </BeliefState>
  <KernelGrammar>
    {{> "definition/process/def-logic-switch"}}
    {{> "definition/process/def-read-and-use-directive"}}
  </KernelGrammar>
  <Contracts>
    {{> "contract/process/artifact-approval-flow"}}
    {{> "contract/process/artifact-approval-marker"}}
    {{> "contract/process/readiness-preflight-gate"}}
    {{> "contract/process/question-rule-slim"}}
    {{> "contract/process/halt-format"}}
  </Contracts>
  <HaltConditions>
    | ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_INTENT` | Repository state and operator message support several materially different routes |
    | `H_SPEC_NOT_APPROVED` | Scaffold targets specs that have not passed approval #1 |
    | `H_V2_INVALID` | A V2 artifact is structurally invalid; return to its authoring owner, never migrate it |
    | `H_WRONG_REPO` | Operator says this is the wrong repository |
  </HaltConditions>
  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_STATE">
      <Goal>Show the exact read-only repository snapshot.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Consume exact result alias `routerState` from the entry skill. Do not repeat `sdd-state`.
        Show its card as a fenced block before the first question. Do not summarize the card into an
        Ask. Emit operator-visible results as live text per `AX_OPERATOR_OUTPUT_LIVE_TEXT`, without
        narrating internal mechanics per `AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION`. Per `AX_STATELESS_FLOW`, this step
        performs no write and creates no hidden resume state. If the operator identifies this as the
        wrong repository, stop with `H_WRONG_REPO`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_CLASSIFY">
      <Goal>Resolve current intent and, only for spec authoring, proportional depth.</Goal>
      <Action>
        A forced intent from a direct skill is authoritative: `scaffold`, `execute`, `critic`, or
        `reconcile`. Preserve the rest of the message as owner payload.

        Otherwise classify from current message plus `routerState`: project-setup · new-scope ·
        evolve-scope · module-decomposition · multi-scope · recover-from-code · execute. Resolve
        scope type for scope work. Ask one concise question only when alternatives would change the
        owner or artifact boundary.

        Apply the artifact reader test from `AX_READER_WITHOUT_SESSION_CONTEXT`: the selected owner
        must produce artifacts understandable without memory of this conversation.

        When alternatives exist, apply `AX_DIVERGE_BEFORE_RECOMMEND`; do not collapse them before the
        operator can see the material trade-off. Confirm SCALE only for project/scope/module authoring
        where it changes interview depth per `AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH`.
        Execute, scaffold, critic, reconcile, and recovery do not need SCALE.

        Apply `READINESS_PREFLIGHT_GATE` once to the read-only snapshot. Missing repository gate
        scripts return to their owning infrastructure/spec authoring path; they never create a
        session or migration branch.

        `FLOW_VERSION=v1` may route to the explicit V1→V2 migration directive after operator
        confirmation. `FLOW_VERSION=v2` never routes to migration. Invalid V2 structure is
        `H_V2_INVALID` and returns to the relevant V2 authoring owner.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_ROUTE">
      <Goal>Load exactly one owner.</Goal>
      <Action>
        <LOGIC_SWITCH>
          WHEN flow version is v1 AND operator explicitly requests migration
            -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/migration-v1-v2.directive.xml")
          WHEN forced intent = scaffold
            -> require well-formed, semantically current approval #1 markers in actual specs, else `H_SPEC_NOT_APPROVED`; READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/scaffold.directive.xml")
          WHEN forced intent = execute OR intent = execute
            -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/execute.directive.xml")
          WHEN forced intent = critic
            -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/critic.directive.xml")
          WHEN forced intent = reconcile
            -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/reconcile.directive.xml")
          WHEN intent = project-setup
            -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/root.directive.xml")
          WHEN intent = recover-from-code
            -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/discover-from-code.directive.xml")
          WHEN intent = module-decomposition
            -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/module.directive.xml")
          WHEN intent in {new-scope, evolve-scope, multi-scope} AND scope-type = infrastructure
            -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/infra.directive.xml")
          WHEN intent in {new-scope, evolve-scope, multi-scope} AND scope-type = interface
            -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/interface.directive.xml")
          WHEN intent in {new-scope, evolve-scope, multi-scope} AND scope-type in {product, library}
            -> READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/scope.directive.xml")
          OTHERWISE -> H_AMBIGUOUS_INTENT
        </LOGIC_SWITCH>
        Per `AX_STATELESS_ARTIFACT`, multi-scope work processes scopes in dependency order and obtains approval #1 for the complete
        changed spec set. It is iteration over owners, not another workflow or session. Any durable
        choice recorded by the selected owner follows `AX_DECISION_LOG_NON_OBVIOUS`: Decision Log
        captures only non-obvious trade-offs, exceptions, and accepted risks.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>
</SddRouter>
